A list that is followed by a blank line is given that blank line.

md reports the list of this document as L3-5 and slices it as
"- a\n- b\n\n". The list holds lines 3 and 4. Line 5 is blank and
belongs to no block: the paragraph below it starts on line 6, and md
says so.

The blank line ends the list, and cmark hands back an end_line that has
already moved on to it, so the whole range is one line too long. Every
blank line under the list is taken: two blank lines give L3-6. No other
block type does this. A heading, a paragraph, a code block, a
blockquote, a table and a thematic break all end on their last line of
content, and a list at the end of a document ends correctly too, which
is why the defect needs a blank line under the list to show up.

Both symptoms:
  blocks-does-not-give-a-list-the-blank-line-below-it (the summary)
  blocks-prints-a-list-without-the-blank-line-below-it (the content)
